Remove obsolete big-endian special case from fts3corrupt4.test

Since check-in 1a888ea60be20a80 ("Improved detection of corrupt freelist
chains on btree pages", released in 3.53.3) page 1 of the test database,
which has a freeblock of size 0, is rejected by btreeComputeFreeSpace().
The CREATE TABLE of the t1_stat table done by "merge=1" therefore fails
on all platforms, independent of the PRNG byte sequence, so tests 25.6a
and 25.6b expect the same result on big-endian as on little-endian
platforms.  See
https://sqlite.org/forum/forumpost/af4461a71d0f935cdefb807a0ca0af9742a714200090ebf64b0de5b760574505

--- a/test/fts3corrupt4.test
+++ b/test/fts3corrupt4.test
@@ -4403,31 +4403,12 @@
     INSERT INTO t1( a ) SELECT randomblob(3000) FROM t2 ;
 } {0 {}}
 
-if {$tcl_platform(byteOrder)=="littleEndian"} {
-  # The SQLITE_CORRUPT error depends on the specific random byte
-  # sequence generated by SQLite's PRNG.  But the SQLite PRNG
-  # uses ChaCha20, which generates a different byte sequence on
-  # big-endian and little-endian platforms.  The SQLITE_CORRUPT
-  # error only comes up when the pseudo-random byte sequence is
-  # the one generated on little-endian platforms.
-  #
-  # See Forum thread:
-  # https://sqlite.org/forum/forumpost/b5f89d813babfd88
-  #
-  do_catchsql_test 25.6a {
-    INSERT INTO t1(t1) SELECT x FROM t2;
-  } {1 {database disk image is malformed}}
-  do_catchsql_test 25.6b {
-    INSERT INTO t1(t1) SELECT x FROM t2;
-  } {1 {database disk image is malformed}}
-} else {
-  do_catchsql_test 25.6a {
-    INSERT INTO t1(t1) SELECT x FROM t2;
-  } {0 {}}
-  do_catchsql_test 25.6b {
-    INSERT INTO t1(t1) SELECT x FROM t2;
-  } {0 {}}
-}
+do_catchsql_test 25.6a {
+  INSERT INTO t1(t1) SELECT x FROM t2;
+} {1 {database disk image is malformed}}
+do_catchsql_test 25.6b {
+  INSERT INTO t1(t1) SELECT x FROM t2;
+} {1 {database disk image is malformed}}
 
 
 #-------------------------------------------------------------------------
